      "body": "# PR type\n\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nFixes #10336\n\nConcurrent checkpoint updates share `last-checkpoint.tmp`, allowing one caller to publish another caller's target or delete its staging link during failure cleanup. Give each update a UUID-based staging path and clean it up only after that caller successfully creates the symlink, while preserving atomic `os.replace` publication and relative link targets.\n\nDocument the existing publication-order semantics: the last successful replacement wins, regardless of checkpoint step or save start order.\n\n## Experiment results\n\n- One focused regression test completes a second update while the first updater's staging link is pending, using nested calls to the real helper and real filesystem operations. The overlapping-success case fails against the original implementation and passes with this fix.\n- Two subtests cover successful overlapping publication and an injected outer replacement failure, checking the published targets and absence of leftover staging links.\n- `python -m pytest tests/utils/test_io_utils.py -q`: **7 passed, 2 subtests passed** (Python 3.12).\n- `python -m pre_commit run --files swift/utils/io_utils.py tests/utils/test_io_utils.py`: **passed**.\n- `git diff --check`: **passed**.\n- Full trainer integration and multi-process checkpoint-saving tests were not run. The regression controls the operation interleaving without threads.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
